{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:admissible-system","kind":"definition","title":"Monomial ordering and admissible system","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-monomial-basis"],"tags":["groebner-basis","ordering","admissible"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder","text":"admissible-system.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/admissible-system.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:admissible-system\"></a><p>A <em>monomial ordering</em> for a <a href=\"#def:monomial-basis\">monomial basis</a>\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> of an algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is a well-ordering <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">&#x3C;</code> on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> such that for\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b, b', r, s \\in B</code>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b &#x3C; b'</code> then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\cdot b \\cdot s &#x3C; r \\cdot b' \\cdot s</code>\nwhenever <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r \\cdot b \\cdot s \\neq 0</code> and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{LM}(r \\cdot b' \\cdot s) \\neq 0</code>.</li>\n<li>If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b' = \\mathrm{LM}(r \\cdot b \\cdot s) \\neq 0</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">r</code> or\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s \\neq 1</code>, then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b &#x3C; \\mathrm{LM}(b')</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B</code> admits a monomial ordering <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">&#x3C;</code>, then the pair <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> is an\n<strong>admissible system</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Divisibility.</strong> If <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> is an admissible system and\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0 \\neq f \\in A</code>, we say <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in B</code> <em>divides</em> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">f</code> (written\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\mid f</code>) if there exist <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">u, v \\in B</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda \\in R^*</code>\nsuch that</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\lambda\\,\\mathrm{LT}(u \\cdot \\beta \\cdot v) = \\mathrm{LT}(f).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/admissible-system.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"2.2.4"}
